# The Ghidra project and the three original executables. Not ours to
# redistribute, and the .rep is a database rather than a reviewable file -
# its findings reach the repository through reverse/exports/ instead.
# See CLAUDE.md rules 7 and 11.
reverse/ghidra/

# Generated from the database, one directory per program (rule 7).
reverse/exports/*/*map.txt

# Depacked images are derived from a binary we do not redistribute, so
# they are not ours to publish either. The depacker in tools/unpack/ and
# the notes beside it are what travel; the bytes are regenerated with
# `py -3.10 tools/unpack/xcur_unpack.py`.
#
# xcursion.json IS committed: it is a handful of recovered header fields,
# not image data, and it is what says which load segment a regenerated
# dump must use.
reverse/unpacked/*.bin
reverse/unpacked/*.EXE
reverse/unpacked/*.exe

# Assets pulled out of a depacked image - the music module and anything
# like it - stand on the same footing: derived from a binary we do not
# redistribute, and the authors' work rather than ours. The extractor in
# tools/ and the notes beside it are what travel.
reverse/unpacked/*.s3m
reverse/unpacked/*.mod
reverse/unpacked/*.xm

# The MCP server registrations. One machine's layout, and two of the
# three servers live outside this repository, so no relative path or
# variable makes it portable. .mcp.json.example IS committed: copy it
# and fill in the paths. CLAUDE.md rule 2.1 for the port that matters.
.mcp.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editors
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user

# Build output, once src/ exists. ANCHORED, and no bare *.exe or *.obj.
#
# An unanchored *.exe matches DIRECTORIES too, and the export directories
# are named after their program - so `*.exe` silently excluded the whole
# of reverse/exports/XCURSION_U.EXE/. Keep build-output patterns pinned
# to where the build actually puts things.
/build/
/src/Debug/
/src/Release/
/src/*.obj
/src/*.exe

# Scratch
*.tmp
*.bak
*.log

# The MSVC port. Build output and vendored third-party libraries.
/build/
/src/.vs/
/src/*.user
/src/third_party/
